> [!MARKS] 4 + 4 = 8 Marks
> **a) Recursion vs Iteration (`4m`):** Side-by-side comparison across 6 parameters | **b) Recursive Tower of Hanoi (`4m`):** Complete C program + `n = 3` trace (`7` moves).

### a) Recursion vs Iteration (4 Marks)

> [!COMPARE] Recursion vs Iteration
> | Parameter | Recursion | Iteration |
> |---|---|---|
> | **Mechanism** | A function repeatedly **calls itself** on smaller subproblems. | A loop construct (`for`, `while`, `do-while`) repeats a block. |
> | **Termination** | Stops when an explicit **base case** is reached. | Stops when the **loop continuation condition** becomes false (`0`). |
> | **Memory Usage** | **`O(depth)` stack space**—pushes one activation frame per call. | **`O(1)` auxiliary stack space**—reuses fixed local variables. |
> | **Execution Speed** | Slightly slower due to function-call/return frame overhead. | Faster—executes lightweight CPU branch instructions. |
> | **Failure Mode** | Missing base case causes runtime **Stack Overflow** crash. | Buggy update causes an **infinite loop** (CPU hang, fixed memory). |
> | **Best Suited For** | Tree/graph traversals, Quick/Merge Sort, Tower of Hanoi. | Linear array scans, counting, iterative DP tables. |

### b) Recursive Function & Program for Tower of Hanoi (4 Marks)

```c
#include <stdio.h>

void towerOfHanoi(int n, char src, char aux, char dest) {
    if (n == 1) {
        printf("Move disk 1 from %c -> %c\n", src, dest);
        return; /* base case */
    }
    towerOfHanoi(n - 1, src, dest, aux);               /* Step 1: n-1 to aux */
    printf("Move disk %d from %c -> %c\n", n, src, dest); /* Step 2: nth to dest */
    towerOfHanoi(n - 1, aux, src, dest);               /* Step 3: n-1 to dest */
}

int main(void) {
    int n = 3;
    towerOfHanoi(n, 'A', 'B', 'C');
    return 0;
}
```

- **Output for `n = 3` (`2³ - 1 = 7` moves):**
  `D1: A->C`, `D2: A->B`, `D1: C->B`, `D3: A->C`, `D1: B->A`, `D2: B->C`, `D1: A->C` (`T(n) = 2ⁿ - 1` moves, `O(2ⁿ)` time).
